# Tailwind CSS Rules

## Responsibilities

- Define design tokens and utility usage patterns
- Prevent arbitrary values and class soup
- Standardize responsive, dark mode, and state variants

## Best Practices

- Use **CSS variables** in `globals.css` for theme tokens (shadcn pattern)
- Extend theme in `tailwind.config.ts`, not inline arbitrary values
- **`cn()` utility** (clsx + tailwind-merge) for conditional classes
- Mobile-first responsive: base → `sm:` → `md:` → `lg:` → `xl:`
- Dark mode via `class` strategy on `<html>` element
- Group related utilities: layout → spacing → typography → color → effects

## Coding Standards

```tsx
// Use cn() for conditional classes
import { cn } from '@/lib/utils';

<div className={cn(
  'flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg border px-4 py-2',
  'bg-card text-card-foreground',
  'hover:bg-accent transition-colors',
  isActive && 'border-primary bg-primary/10',
  className
)} />
```

- Max ~10 utility classes per element; extract to component if exceeded
- Use `@apply` sparingly in globals.css for base resets only
- Semantic color tokens: `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `border-border`
- Never hardcode hex colors in components

## Folder Structure

```
src/app/globals.css       # CSS variables, base layer
tailwind.config.ts        # Theme extension
src/lib/utils.ts          # cn() helper
```

## Naming Convention

- Component wrapper classes: component name as comment, not BEM
- Custom utilities in tailwind config: `legal-*` prefix if needed

## Performance Rules

- Purge unused classes (Tailwind JIT handles this)
- Avoid animating layout properties (width, height, top, left)

## Security Rules

- N/A for styling layer

## Theme Tokens (Dark First)

```css
/* globals.css — reference values */
--background: 224 71% 4%;      /* near-black blue */
--foreground: 213 31% 91%;
--primary: 210 100% 52%;         /* accent blue */
--muted: 223 47% 11%;
--border: 216 34% 17%;
--destructive: 0 63% 51%;
--success: 142 76% 36%;
--warning: 38 92% 50%;
```

## Examples

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — Semantic tokens, responsive
<main className="flex-1 overflow-y-auto p-4 md:p-6 lg:p-8">
  <h1 className="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground">
    Cases
  </h1>
</main>

// ❌ BAD — Arbitrary values, hardcoded colors
<div className="bg-[#1a1a2e] p-[13px] text-[#eee]">
```

## Things to Avoid

- Inline `style={{}}` when Tailwind utilities exist
- Duplicating responsive breakpoints inconsistently
- `!important` overrides
- Mixing Tailwind with CSS modules in same component
- Long unreadable class strings — extract component

## Checklist Before Finishing Any Task

- [ ] Uses semantic color tokens, not raw colors
- [ ] Dark mode variants tested
- [ ] Responsive breakpoints applied
- [ ] `cn()` used for conditional classes
- [ ] No arbitrary values without justification
- [ ] Focus/hover/active states styled
